[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"209","stub":{"id":"209","section":"Park Boundary/ Gateway to Dinley Bridge","altname":"Gateway","river":"Kaweah","difficulty":"IVtoV","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"829","dateTime":"2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"111096","location":{"latitude":"36.4849","longitude":"-118.835"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"116363","location":{"latitude":"36.4586","longitude":"-118.876"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"3","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"364","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2705","description":"Winding our way, like a pinball, through the bumpers of Lithium.  100  points per bump, 1000 when lit.  Hey, if this rapid were suddenly frozen, would we have Freestyle Skiiing moguls?","caption":"Pinball Wizard meets Whitewater Rafting.  \"Can you say....Rock Garden?\"","poi_name":"Lithium (a.k.a. Bumper); Class IV+","subject":"ABLE?  Is that just wishful thinking?  Matt Urdan in the All Outdoors Raft takes on the Kaweah outside Sequoia National Park","author":"Beyond Limits Whitewater Rafting","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/364","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/364"}},{"id":"366","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2705","description":"Winding our way like a pinball through the bumpers of Lithium, 100 points per bump--1000 when lit.  Hey, if this rapid were suddenly frozen, would we have Freestyle Skiing Moguls?","caption":"Pinball Wizard meets Whitewater Rafting.","poi_name":"Lithium (a.k.a. Bumper); Class IV+","subject":"ABLE?  Is that just wishful thinking?  Matt Urdan in the All Outdoors raft takes on the Kaweah outside Sequoia National Park.","author":"Beyond Limits Whitewater Rafting","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/366","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/366"}}],"detail":{"id":"209","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"The Park Boundary/Gateway section of the Kaweah is a wonderfully busy river.\n\nThe rapids are long, steep, steady and bouldery. Boaters stepping up into class 5 rivers will find no better learning ground than the Kaweah River.\n\n**Put in:**\n\nGateway Bridge was the traditional put-in, but because of concerns by the downstream land owner, the limited parking along the road has been posted for no parking. Creative kayakers still find ways of launching here at times, but there are other options a short ways downstream.\n\nYou can also drive upstream to Southern CA Edison Road, or into the National Park, but the rapids upstream of Gateway are a bit more difficult and may require one portage.\n\n**Take out:**\n\nDinely Bridge\n\nHere is a video of the Park Boundary section as well as two rapids in the Gateway section (The Chute and Powerhouse).\n\nThe video gives each rapid in order from top to bottom.  The missing rapids are class II-III in nature.\n\n[Click To Play](http://blip.tv/file/get/Kayak559-KaweahParkBoundary866.m4v)\n\nThe following video features sections of the Park Boundary, Gateway, Dinley, and Lake run of the Kaweah.  It was shot and edited by Daniel Lundburg.\n\n[Click To Play](http://blip.tv/file/get/Kayak559-KaweahRiver3302008758.m4v)\n\n**Other Information Sources:**\n\nSee Bill Pooley's [Kaweah River Page](http://www.c2.com/kaweah/) for a huge assortment of resources and information about the Kaweah River.\n\n[Cacreeks.com](http://www.cacreeks.com/kaweah.htm)\n\nThe Chute: [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DQKy1lo4RJU](http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DQKy1lo4RJU)\n\nBumper: [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=skFjDekP8AU](http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=skFjDekP8AU)","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"3.6","correlations":[{"reachID":"209","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"500","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"3000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"KAWEAH RIVER AT THREE RIVERS","gaugeSource":"CDEC","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"TRR","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"829","dateTime":"2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":null,"location":{"latitude":"36.4439","longitude":"-118.9044"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://cdec.water.ca.gov/dynamicapp/QueryF?s=TRR","text":"California Data Exchange - Station Log"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://cdec.water.ca.gov/cdecplotter/JspPlotAll?staid_id=TRR","text":"California Data Exchange - Data Plot"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":"gauge is upstream of the NF confluence","status":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"829","dateTime":"2026-05-12T00:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["111096","116363"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-118.835747,36.484669],[-118.835653,36.484366],[-118.835698,36.48421],[-118.83594,36.483942],[-118.83641,36.483814],[-118.836684,36.483651],[-118.837168,36.483116],[-118.837378,36.481566],[-118.83742,36.481229],[-118.837576,36.480683],[-118.837502,36.480293],[-118.837548,36.479991],[-118.837834,36.479567],[-118.837955,36.479507],[-118.838513,36.479362],[-118.838798,36.479233],[-118.838864,36.479147],[-118.838984,36.479123],[-118.839258,36.47907],[-118.839509,36.479132],[-118.840054,36.479394],[-118.840534,36.479